   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evidence generation on the multidimensional performance of agriculture using TAPE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of TAPE implementation are the following:
- To assess the current level of agroecology adoption within a projects or across various regions and agricultural activities of the country. The assessment is a starting point for policy recommendations and can be used as a baseline for a further assessment a few years later if needed.
- To assess the sustainability of food producers regarding TAPE core criteria on economic, environment, health and nutrition, social and governance dimensions.
- To identify barriers and challenges in implementing sustainable approaches and propose strategies to overcome them with the FAO 10 Elements of Agroecology as an entry point for food system transformation.
-    To provide valuable data for policymakers, researchers, and farmers to guide decision-making and promote sustainable agricultural policies and programmes
-   To generate robust evidence on the contribution of agroecology in the transformation to sustainable agriculture and food systems, through the collection and comparative analysis of multidimensional data at multiple locations and under different contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
